IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wim-dates`

-- Workplace Injury Management and Workers Compensation Act 1998 (NSW) -- the injured worker's claim, from notice of the
-- injury to the insurer's decision, and the rules on stopping weekly payments.
--
-- SEAT: the injured worker making a new claim (Chapter 7). Every exported question is one the worker would ask: "Am I a
-- worker?", "Must I give notice?", "By when must I claim?", "By when must the insurer start my payments?", "By when must
-- it decide my claim?", "How much notice must I get before my payments stop?", "Must my employer give me suitable work?".
-- The insurer, the employer, the Authority, the Commission and its President get no seat: their decisions and findings
-- are asked as facts, and what they must do is encoded as what it means for the worker (a date, a stop, a payment).
--
-- Provisions: s 4(1) (worker, injury); s 42 (significant injury) with s 45(1); s 44(1); s 48, s 48A; s 49; s 119(1)-(4)
-- with s 324(2); ss 254-256 (notice of injury); s 261 (time for a claim); s 280A; ss 266-270 (provisional weekly
-- payments); ss 274-276, 279, 280 (deciding weekly and medical claims); ss 281, 282 (lump sum and work injury damages
-- claims); ss 80, 84 (notice before weekly payments stop or are reduced).
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no question answers JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no ("means", "unless", "only
-- if", "does not include", "cannot", a period the text fixes), or NOTHING where the Act does not answer on the facts
-- given; each NOTHING carries a "NOTHING-kind" comment. Questions phrased "Does section X stop me ...?" answer only for
-- that section; other sections, and the Workers Compensation Act 1987, may still stop the claim.
--
-- Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website (as collected by the Open Australian Legal Corpus on
-- 10 March 2025; unofficial, possibly out of date). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Claims under the Workplace Injury Management and Workers Compensation Act 1998`

§§ `Am I a worker, and is it an injury (s 4)`

-- s 4(1) "worker means a person who has entered into or works under a contract of service or a training contract with
-- an employer ... However, it does not include -- (a) a member of the NSW Police Force who is a contributor to the Police
-- Superannuation Fund ..., (b) a person whose employment is casual (that is for 1 period only of not more than 5 working
-- days) and who is employed otherwise than for the purposes of the employer's trade or business, (c) an officer of a
-- religious or other voluntary association who is employed upon duties for the association outside the officer's
-- ordinary working hours, ... if the officer's remuneration from the association does not exceed $700 per year, or
-- (d) except as provided by Schedule 1, a registered participant of a sporting organisation ...". s 5: "Schedule 1 has
-- effect" (deemed workers), which this encoding does not work out: where it may apply, NOTHING.
@export Am I a worker covered by the NSW workers compensation scheme (s 4 definition of worker)?
GIVEN `I work under a contract of service or a training contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a contract of service (employment, written, oral or implied) or an apprenticeship or traineeship contract with the employer
      `Schedule 1 may deem me a worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you may fall in one of the deemed-worker cases of Schedule 1 (for example labour hire, outworkers, some contractors, rural workers, jockeys, ministers of religion); this encoding does not decide them
      `I am a NSW police officer contributing to the Police Superannuation Fund` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a member of the NSW Police Force who contributes to the Police Superannuation Fund (closed to new members in 1988)
      `my work is one casual stint of 5 working days or less outside the employer's business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your work is casual, for one period only of not more than 5 working days, and not for the purposes of the employer's trade or business
      `I am a religious or voluntary association officer working outside my ordinary hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an officer of a religious or other voluntary association doing its duties outside your ordinary working hours
      `my yearly pay from that association` IS A NUMBER @desc Your remuneration from that association, in dollars per year (0 if none or not applicable)
      `I am a registered sporting participant paid only for taking part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a registered participant of a sporting organisation injured while taking part, training or travelling for it, and paid only for those things
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I a worker` MEANS
    IF `I work under a contract of service or a training contract`
    THEN BRANCH IF `I am a NSW police officer contributing to the Police Superannuation Fund` THEN JUST FALSE
                IF `my work is one casual stint of 5 working days or less outside the employer's business` THEN JUST FALSE
                IF     `I am a religious or voluntary association officer working outside my ordinary hours`
                   AND `my yearly pay from that association` AT MOST 700
                THEN JUST FALSE
                IF `I am a registered sporting participant paid only for taking part`
                THEN IF `Schedule 1 may deem me a worker`
                     THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text: Schedule 1, not encoded here)
                     ELSE JUST FALSE
                OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `Schedule 1 may deem me a worker`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text: Schedule 1, not encoded here)
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 4(1) "injury -- (a) means a personal injury arising out of or in the course of employment, and (b) includes -- (i) a
-- disease contracted by a worker in the course of employment, where the employment was a contributing factor to the
-- disease, or (ii) the aggravation, acceleration, exacerbation or deterioration of any disease, where the employment was a
-- contributing factor ..., but (c) does not include (except in the case of a worker employed in or about a mine) -- (i) a
-- dust disease, or (ii) the aggravation ... of a dust disease." (The 1987 Act's own s 4 asks for the "main contributing
-- factor" for a disease injury: finding 1 in NOTES.md.)
@export Is what happened to me an injury under this Act (s 4 definition of injury)?
GIVEN `a personal injury arising out of or in the course of my employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you suffered a personal injury arising out of, or in the course of, your employment
      `a disease I caught in the course of employment, to which the employment contributed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you contracted a disease in the course of your employment, the employment being a contributing factor
      `a disease made worse, the employment contributing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a disease you have was aggravated, accelerated, exacerbated or made to deteriorate, the employment being a contributing factor
      `it is a dust disease or a worsening of one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a dust disease (as in the Workers' Compensation (Dust Diseases) Act 1942) or the aggravation of one
      `I am employed in or about a mine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are employed in or about a mine
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is it an injury` MEANS
    BRANCH IF     `it is a dust disease or a worsening of one`
              AND (NOT `I am employed in or about a mine`)
           THEN JUST FALSE
           IF    `a personal injury arising out of or in the course of my employment`
              OR `a disease I caught in the course of employment, to which the employment contributed`
              OR `a disease made worse, the employment contributing`
           THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `Injury management (Chapter 3)`

-- s 42(1) "significant injury means a workplace injury that is likely to result in the worker being incapacitated for
-- work for a continuous period of more than 7 days, whether or not any of those days are work days". s 45(1) "When it
-- appears that a workplace injury is a significant injury, an insurer ... must establish an injury management plan for
-- the injured worker." (The "when" is a "where" under the ruling of 5 November 2026: when it fails, JUST FALSE.)
@export Must the insurer set up an injury management plan for me (ss 42, 45)?
GIVEN `the days in a row I am likely to be unable to work, fully or partly` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days in a row (counting non-work days) you are likely to be wholly or partly unable to work because of the injury, as it appears at the time
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must the insurer make me an injury management plan` MEANS
    IF `the days in a row I am likely to be unable to work, fully or partly` GREATER THAN 7
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 49(1) "If a worker who has been totally or partially incapacitated for work as a result of an injury is able to
-- return to work ..., the employer liable to pay compensation ... must at the request of the worker provide suitable
-- employment for the worker." (3) "This section does not apply if -- (a) it is not reasonably practicable ..., or (b)
-- the worker voluntarily left the employment of that employer after the injury happened ..., or (c) the employer
-- terminated the worker's employment after the injury happened, other than for the reason that the worker was not fit
-- for employment as a result of the injury."
@export Must my employer give me suitable work (s 49)?
GIVEN `I was unable to work, fully or partly, because of the injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury left you totally or partially incapacitated for work
      `I am able to return to work, full-time or part-time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are now able to return to work (full-time or part-time, in your old job or another)
      `I have asked my employer for suitable work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have asked the employer liable to compensate you to provide suitable employment
      `it is not reasonably practicable for the employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is found not reasonably practicable for the employer to provide such employment
      `I left that employer voluntarily after the injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you voluntarily left that employer's employment after the injury happened
      `the employer dismissed me after the injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer ended your employment after the injury happened
      `the reason was that the injury left me unfit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you were dismissed: whether the reason was that you were not fit for the employment because of the injury
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must my employer give me suitable work` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `I was unable to work, fully or partly, because of the injury`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF (NOT `I am able to return to work, full-time or part-time`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF (NOT `I have asked my employer for suitable work`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `it is not reasonably practicable for the employer` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `I left that employer voluntarily after the injury` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF     `the employer dismissed me after the injury`
              AND (NOT `the reason was that the injury left me unfit`)
           THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Returning to work (ss 48, 48A)`

-- s 48A(2)(b): "weekly payments to the worker will be suspended from the date specified in the notice which must be a
-- date at least 14 days after notice is given but no more than 60 days after notice is given".
@export Is the suspension date in my return-to-work notice allowed (s 48A(2)(b))?
GIVEN `the day the notice was given to me` IS A DATE @desc The day the insurer gave you the written notice under s 48A(2)
      `the suspension date in the notice` IS A DATE @desc The date from which the notice says your weekly payments will be suspended
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my suspension date allowed` MEANS
    IF     `the days` AT LEAST 14
       AND `the days` AT MOST 60
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `the days` MEANS `the days from` `the day the notice was given to me` `to` `the suspension date in the notice`

-- s 48(1): a worker with current work capacity "must ... make reasonable efforts to return to work"; s 48(2) treats
-- waiting periods as reasonable efforts. s 48A(1)-(7): suspension after written notice, 28 days of suspension, resumption
-- with the suspended payments forfeited, termination, and cessation where in the last 12 months there were 2 notices
-- without a suspension or 1 suspension.
DECLARE `What the insurer may do under s 48A` IS ONE OF
    `nothing under section 48A`
    `give me a written notice first, stating the obligation and a suspension date`
    `suspend my weekly payments for 28 days from the date in the notice`
    `resume my weekly payments from the day I complied, the suspended payments being forfeited`
    `terminate my weekly payments for this injury`
    `cease and determine my entitlement to weekly payments for this injury`

@export What may the insurer do to my weekly payments if I do not make reasonable efforts to return to work (ss 48, 48A)?
GIVEN `I have current work capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have current work capacity (some capacity for suitable work), as defined in Schedule 3 to the 1987 Act
      `I am making reasonable efforts to return to work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are making reasonable efforts, with the employer or insurer, to return to suitable or pre-injury work (time spent waiting for a rehabilitation service, a reply to your request for work, or offered work to start counts as reasonable efforts)
      `the insurer has given me a written notice under s 48A(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has given you a written notice naming the obligation, a suspension date and the consequences
      `I complied by the date in the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you complied with the obligation named in the notice before the suspension date
      `I complied during the 28-day suspension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you complied during the 28 days of suspension
      `the 28-day suspension has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the 28 days of suspension after the date in the notice have passed
      `notices without a suspension in the 12 months before` IS A NUMBER @desc How many s 48A(2) notices you were given in the 12 months before this notice that were not followed by a suspension
      `suspensions in the 12 months before` IS A NUMBER @desc How many times your weekly payments were suspended under s 48A(3) in the 12 months before this notice
GIVETH A `What the insurer may do under s 48A`
`What may the insurer do if I do not try to return to work` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `I have current work capacity`) THEN `nothing under section 48A`
           IF `I am making reasonable efforts to return to work` THEN `nothing under section 48A`
           IF (NOT `the insurer has given me a written notice under s 48A(2)`) THEN `give me a written notice first, stating the obligation and a suspension date`
           IF `I complied by the date in the notice` THEN `nothing under section 48A`
           IF `I complied during the 28-day suspension` THEN `resume my weekly payments from the day I complied, the suspended payments being forfeited`
           IF (NOT `the 28-day suspension has ended`) THEN `suspend my weekly payments for 28 days from the date in the notice`
           IF    `notices without a suspension in the 12 months before` AT LEAST 2
              OR `suspensions in the 12 months before` AT LEAST 1
           THEN `cease and determine my entitlement to weekly payments for this injury`
           OTHERWISE `terminate my weekly payments for this injury`

§§ `Medical examinations (ss 119, 324)`

-- s 119(1), (2): a worker "must, if so required by the employer, submit himself or herself for examination by a medical
-- practitioner, provided and paid by the employer"; (3) refusal or obstruction suspends "the worker's right to recover
-- compensation ... or ... to the weekly payments ... until the examination has taken place"; (4) "A worker must not be
-- required to submit ... otherwise than in accordance with the Workers Compensation Guidelines". s 324(2) the same for an
-- examination a medical assessor requires.
@export Are my rights to compensation and weekly payments suspended because of a medical examination (ss 119, 324)?
GIVEN `I was required to be examined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer (or the insurer for it), or a medical assessor, required you to attend a medical examination
      `a medical assessor required it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the requirement came from a medical assessor of the Personal Injury Commission (rather than from your employer)
      `the requirement followed the Workers Compensation Guidelines` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an employer's requirement: whether it was made in accordance with the Workers Compensation Guidelines (including how often)
      `I refused or obstructed the examination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you refused to attend or in any way obstructed the examination
      `the examination has since taken place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the examination has now taken place
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Are my compensation rights suspended for an examination` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `I was required to be examined`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF     (NOT `a medical assessor required it`)
              AND (NOT `the requirement followed the Workers Compensation Guidelines`)
           THEN JUST FALSE
           IF (NOT `I refused or obstructed the examination`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the examination has since taken place` THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Notice of injury (ss 44, 254-256)`

-- s 44(1) "An injured worker must notify the employer that the worker has received a workplace injury as soon as possible
-- after the injury happens." s 254(1) "Neither compensation nor work injury damages are recoverable by an injured worker
-- unless notice of the injury is given to the employer as soon as possible after the injury happened and before the
-- worker has voluntarily left the employment in which the worker was at the time of the injury." (2) not a bar "if in
-- proceedings ... it is found that there are special circumstances"; (3)(a)-(g) and (4)(a)-(c) list them. s 256(4) an
-- entry in the register of injuries made as soon as possible "is sufficient notice of the injury".
@export Does the notice-of-injury rule stop me recovering compensation or work injury damages (s 254)?
GIVEN `I told my employer about the injury as soon as possible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave notice of the injury (orally or in writing, to the employer, a person it designated or your supervisor) as soon as possible after it happened
      `I told them before I voluntarily left that job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that notice was given before you voluntarily left the job you had when injured (yes if you have not left)
      `the injury went in the register of injuries as soon as possible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether particulars of the injury were entered in the workplace register of injuries as soon as possible after it happened
      `my employer was not prejudiced by the missing or faulty notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is found that the employer (or other defendant) was not prejudiced by the lack of notice or by a defect in it
      `the failure was due to ignorance, mistake, absence from NSW or other reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is found that the lack of (or defect in) notice came from ignorance, mistake, absence from the State or another reasonable cause
      `my employer knew of the injury at or about the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer (or other defendant) knew of the injury from any source at or about the time it happened
      `my employer reported the injury to the Nominal Insurer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer reported the injury to the Nominal Insurer (icare) as the Act requires
      `my employer breached s 231 (the summary of the Act and insurance details)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer contravened s 231, for example by not displaying the summary of the Act and its insurance details
      `the injury was treated in a first aid room at work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury was treated in a first aid room at your place of work
      `the employer reported it to a mines or WHS inspector, as owner of a mine or quarry or occupier of a factory, workshop, office or shop` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer owns a mine or quarry, or occupies a factory, workshop, office or shop, and reported the injury (or had it reported) to an inspector of mines or a Work Health and Safety inspector
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does the notice rule stop me` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the injury went in the register of injuries as soon as possible` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF     `I told my employer about the injury as soon as possible`
              AND `I told them before I voluntarily left that job`
           THEN JUST FALSE
           IF    `my employer was not prejudiced by the missing or faulty notice`
              OR `the failure was due to ignorance, mistake, absence from NSW or other reasonable cause`
              OR `my employer knew of the injury at or about the time`
              OR `my employer reported the injury to the Nominal Insurer`
              OR `my employer breached s 231 (the summary of the Act and insurance details)`
              OR `the injury was treated in a first aid room at work`
              OR `the employer reported it to a mines or WHS inspector, as owner of a mine or quarry or occupier of a factory, workshop, office or shop`
           THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `The time for a claim (s 261)`

-- s 261(6) "If an injured worker first becomes aware that he or she has received an injury after the injury was received,
-- the injury is for the purposes of this section taken to have been received when the worker first became so aware."
GIVEN `the day of the injury` IS A DATE, `I only became aware of the injury later` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day I became aware` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the injury is taken to be received` `the day of the injury` `aware later` `I only became aware of the injury later` `on` `the day I became aware` MEANS
    IF     `I only became aware of the injury later`
       AND `the day of the injury` `is before` `the day I became aware`
    THEN `the day I became aware`
    ELSE `the day of the injury`

-- s 261(1) "Compensation cannot be recovered unless a claim for the compensation has been made within 6 months after the
-- injury or accident happened".
@export By when must I make my claim for workers compensation (s 261(1), (6))?
GIVEN `the day of the injury` IS A DATE @desc The day the injury or accident happened
      `I only became aware of the injury later` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you first became aware that you had been injured some time after the injury (for example a gradual or disease injury)
      `the day I became aware` IS A DATE @desc The day you first became aware you had received the injury (any day if not applicable)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I claim compensation` MEANS
    `the date` 6 `months after` (`the day the injury is taken to be received` `the day of the injury` `aware later` `I only became aware of the injury later` `on` `the day I became aware`)

-- s 261(3) any claim for compensation for the injury counts; (9) an entry in the employer's register of injuries counts
-- as a claim. (4) a late claim is not barred "if it is found that the failure was occasioned by ignorance, mistake,
-- absence from the State or other reasonable cause, and either -- (a) the claim is made within 3 years after the injury
-- ..., or (b) ... the claim is in respect of an injury resulting in the death or serious and permanent disablement of a
-- worker." (5) not barred "if the insurer concerned determines to accept the claim outside that period. An insurer cannot
-- determine to accept a claim made more than 3 years after the injury ... except with the approval of the Authority."
@export Does the 6-month time limit stop me recovering workers compensation (s 261)?
GIVEN `the day of the injury` IS A DATE @desc The day the injury or accident happened
      `I only became aware of the injury later` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you first became aware that you had been injured some time after the injury
      `the day I became aware` IS A DATE @desc The day you first became aware you had received the injury (any day if not applicable)
      `the day of my first claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you first made any claim for compensation for this injury, of any kind, or the injury was entered in your employer's register of injuries, whichever was earlier
      `the delay was due to ignorance, mistake, absence from NSW or other reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is found that claiming late was caused by ignorance, mistake, absence from the State or another reasonable cause
      `the injury left me seriously and permanently disabled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury has resulted in your serious and permanent disablement
      `the insurer decided to accept my late claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has decided to accept the claim even though it was made outside the time
      `the Authority approved that acceptance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the State Insurance Regulatory Authority approved the insurer accepting it (needed where the claim was made more than 3 years after the injury)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does the time limit stop me` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the day of my first claim` `is on or before` (`the date` 6 `months after` `received`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF     `the insurer decided to accept my late claim`
              AND (   `within 3 years`
                   OR `the Authority approved that acceptance`)
           THEN JUST FALSE
           IF     `the delay was due to ignorance, mistake, absence from NSW or other reasonable cause`
              AND (   `within 3 years`
                   OR `the injury left me seriously and permanently disabled`)
           THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `received` MEANS `the day the injury is taken to be received` `the day of the injury` `aware later` `I only became aware of the injury later` `on` `the day I became aware`
        `within 3 years` MEANS `the day of my first claim` `is on or before` (`the date` 3 `years after` `received`)

§§ `Starting provisional weekly payments (ss 266-270)`

-- The parties and acts of the two regulative rules of this encoding (s 267 with s 268 here; s 316 in wim-disputes.l4).
DECLARE `Claim party` IS ONE OF
    `the insurer`
    `the defendant`

DECLARE `Claim act` IS ONE OF
    `commence provisional weekly payments`
    `give written notice of a reasonable excuse`
    `respond to the pre-filing statement`

-- s 267(1) "Provisional weekly payments of compensation by an insurer are to commence within 7 days after initial
-- notification to the insurer of an injury to a worker, unless the insurer has a reasonable excuse"; (2) only an excuse
-- the Workers Compensation Guidelines provide is a reasonable excuse; (5) failing to commence is an offence. s 268 an
-- insurer that does not commence because it has a reasonable excuse "must within 7 days after receiving the initial
-- notification of injury give the worker notice in writing". Time 0 is the day of the initial notification.
GIVEN `the insurer has a reasonable excuse under the Guidelines` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Claim party` `Claim act`
`s 267 and s 268 -- the insurer must start provisional weekly payments, or give notice of its excuse, within 7 days` `the insurer has a reasonable excuse under the Guidelines` MEANS
    IF `the insurer has a reasonable excuse under the Guidelines`
    THEN    (PARTY `the insurer`
             MUST `commence provisional weekly payments`
             WITHIN 7
             LEST BREACH BY `the insurer` BECAUSE "neither payments nor notice of the excuse within 7 days (s 268)")
        ROR (PARTY `the insurer`
             MUST `give written notice of a reasonable excuse`
             WITHIN 7
             LEST BREACH BY `the insurer` BECAUSE "no written notice of the reasonable excuse within 7 days (s 268)")
    ELSE PARTY `the insurer`
         MUST `commence provisional weekly payments`
         WITHIN 7
         LEST BREACH BY `the insurer` BECAUSE "provisional weekly payments not commenced within 7 days of the initial notification (s 267(1), (5))"

-- The helper that runs a duty over what happened. On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not
-- BREACH; so where the act was done, FULFILLED means in time and anything else late; where it was not, the helper asks
-- whether doing it now would still be in time. It takes a DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
DECLARE `What became of the duty` IS ONE OF
    `the duty was kept`
    `the duty was not kept`
    `the duty is still open`

GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Claim party` `Claim act`
      `the party` IS A `Claim party`
      `the act` IS A `Claim act`
      `the act has been done` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time the act was done` IS A NUMBER
      `the time now` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `What became of the duty`
`what became of` `the rule` `for` `the party` `with` `the act` `done` `the act has been done` `at` `the time the act was done` `now` `the time now` MEANS
    IF `the act has been done`
    THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time the act was done`), (EVENT `the party` `the act` `the time the act was done`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `the duty was kept`
         OTHERWISE `the duty was not kept`
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time now`), (EVENT `the party` `the act` `the time now`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `the duty is still open`
         OTHERWISE `the duty was not kept`

@export By when must the insurer start my provisional weekly payments, or tell me in writing why not (ss 267, 268)?
GIVEN `the day the insurer was first notified of my injury` IS A DATE @desc The day of the initial notification of the injury to the insurer (by you, your employer, or someone such as your doctor), in the form the Guidelines require
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must my provisional weekly payments start` MEANS `the date` 7 `days after` `the day the insurer was first notified of my injury`

@export Has the insurer kept its duty to start my provisional weekly payments or tell me its reasonable excuse within 7 days (ss 267, 268)?
GIVEN `the day the insurer was first notified of my injury` IS A DATE @desc The day of the initial notification of the injury to the insurer
      `the insurer has a reasonable excuse under the Guidelines` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has an excuse for not starting payments that the Workers Compensation Guidelines recognise as a reasonable excuse
      `my provisional weekly payments have started` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has started paying you provisional weekly payments
      `the day they started` IS A DATE @desc The day the payments started (any day if they have not)
      `the insurer has told me its excuse in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has given you written notice that it has a reasonable excuse, with its details and how to claim
      `the day of that notice` IS A DATE @desc The day of that written notice (any day if none)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `What became of the duty`
`Has the insurer started my payments in time` MEANS
    IF `my provisional weekly payments have started`
    THEN `what became of` `the rule` `for` `the insurer` `with` `commence provisional weekly payments` `done` TRUE `at` (`day` `the day they started`) `now` (`day` `today`)
    ELSE IF     `the insurer has a reasonable excuse under the Guidelines`
            AND `the insurer has told me its excuse in writing`
         THEN `what became of` `the rule` `for` `the insurer` `with` `give written notice of a reasonable excuse` `done` TRUE `at` (`day` `the day of that notice`) `now` (`day` `today`)
         ELSE `what became of` `the rule` `for` `the insurer` `with` `commence provisional weekly payments` `done` FALSE `at` 0 `now` (`day` `today`)
    WHERE
        `the rule` MEANS `s 267 and s 268 -- the insurer must start provisional weekly payments, or give notice of its excuse, within 7 days` `the insurer has a reasonable excuse under the Guidelines`
        GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE
        GIVETH A NUMBER
        `day` `the date` MEANS max 0 (`the days from` `the day the insurer was first notified of my injury` `to` `the date`)

-- s 270(1) the insurer "may require the worker to provide ... (a) a medical certificate certifying as to the worker's
-- incapacity for work, and (b) a form of authority"; (2) "The insurer may discontinue weekly payments of compensation
-- under this Division if the worker fails to comply with a requirement under this section within 7 days after it is
-- communicated to the worker by the insurer."
@export May the insurer stop my provisional weekly payments because I have not given it a medical certificate or signed authority (s 270)?
GIVEN `the insurer asked me for a certificate or authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has required you to give it a medical certificate of your incapacity, or a signed authority for your treating providers to give it information
      `the day the request reached me` IS A DATE @desc The day the requirement was communicated to you
      `I have provided it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have provided what was required
      `the day I provided it` IS A DATE @desc The day you provided it (any day if not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May the insurer stop my provisional payments for missing papers` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `the insurer asked me for a certificate or authority`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF     `I have provided it`
              AND `the day I provided it` `is on or before` `the last day`
           THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `today` `is on or before` `the last day` THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the last day` MEANS `the date` 7 `days after` `the day the request reached me`

§§ `Deciding my claim (ss 274-282)`

-- s 274(1) "Within 21 days after a claim for weekly payments is made the person on whom the claim is made must determine
-- the claim"; (2), (3) provisional acceptance for up to 12 weeks "operates to extend the period within which the claim
-- must be determined until the end of the period for which liability has been accepted on a provisional basis"; s 275(2)
-- and s 276(1) the same where provisional payments began on the initial notification. An extension never shortens the
-- 21 days (fork F4).
@export By when must the insurer decide my claim for weekly payments (ss 274-276)?
GIVEN `the day I made my claim for weekly payments` IS A DATE @desc The day your claim for weekly payments was made (on the employer or the insurer)
      `the insurer has accepted liability provisionally` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer is paying you on a provisional acceptance of liability (before or after your claim)
      `the last day of the provisional period` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the period (at most 12 weeks) for which the insurer accepted liability provisionally (any day if none)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must my weekly payments claim be decided` MEANS
    IF `the insurer has accepted liability provisionally`
    THEN `the later of` `twenty-one days` `and` `the last day of the provisional period`
    ELSE `twenty-one days`
    WHERE
        `twenty-one days` MEANS `the date` 21 `days after` `the day I made my claim for weekly payments`

-- s 279(1) "Within 21 days after a claim for medical expenses compensation is made the person on whom the claim is made
-- must determine the claim by accepting or disputing liability."
@export By when must the insurer decide my claim for medical expenses (s 279)?
GIVEN `the day I made my claim for medical expenses` IS A DATE @desc The day your claim for medical, hospital or rehabilitation expenses was made
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must my medical expenses claim be decided` MEANS `the date` 21 `days after` `the day I made my claim for medical expenses`

-- s 280(1) provisional acceptance of medical expenses "for an amount of up to $5,000 or such other amount as may be
-- specified by the Workers Compensation Guidelines".
@export Up to how much of my medical expenses can the insurer accept provisionally, before deciding liability (s 280)?
GIVEN `the Guidelines specify another amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Workers Compensation Guidelines in force specify an amount other than $5,000
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much medical expense can be accepted provisionally` MEANS
    IF `the Guidelines specify another amount`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text: the Workers Compensation Guidelines' amount, not deposited)
    ELSE JUST 5000

-- s 280A "A claim for work injury damages in respect of an injury cannot be made unless a claim for lump sum
-- compensation in respect of the injury is made before or at the same time".
@export May I make a claim for work injury damages (s 280A)?
GIVEN `I have claimed lump sum compensation for this injury, before or with this claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made a claim for lump sum (permanent impairment) compensation for the same injury, before or at the same time as the damages claim
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May I claim work injury damages` MEANS
    IF `I have claimed lump sum compensation for this injury, before or with this claim`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 281(2) a lump sum or work injury damages claim must be determined "(a) within 1 month after the degree of permanent
-- impairment first becomes fully ascertainable, as agreed by the parties or as determined by a medical assessor, or (b)
-- within 2 months after the claimant has provided to the insurer all relevant particulars about the claim, whichever is
-- the later." (2A) it "cannot be delayed beyond 2 months after the claimant has provided ... all relevant particulars ...
-- unless the insurer has within that 2-month period notified the claimant that the degree of permanent impairment ... is
-- not fully ascertainable." s 282(2) particulars are not all provided until the worker attends any examination the
-- employer requires.
DECLARE `When my claim must be decided` IS ONE OF
    `by`
        HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `one month after my impairment becomes fully ascertainable, and not before two months after my particulars`
        HAS `the earliest last day` IS A DATE

@export By when must the insurer decide my claim for lump sum compensation or work injury damages, and make an offer if it accepts liability (ss 281, 282)?
GIVEN `the day I gave the insurer all relevant particulars` IS A DATE @desc The day you finished giving the insurer all the relevant particulars of the claim (s 282: the injury, all impairments, earlier injuries or conditions, losses and negligence for damages, previous employment for a lump sum, and attending any examination the employer required)
      `the insurer told me within 2 months that my impairment is not yet fully ascertainable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, within 2 months after those particulars, the insurer notified you that the degree of your permanent impairment is not fully ascertainable
      `my impairment has become fully ascertainable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the degree of your permanent impairment has become fully ascertainable, as agreed with the insurer or as a medical assessor determined
      `the day it became fully ascertainable` IS A DATE @desc The day the degree of permanent impairment first became fully ascertainable (any day if it has not)
GIVETH A `When my claim must be decided`
`By when must my lump sum or damages claim be decided` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `the insurer told me within 2 months that my impairment is not yet fully ascertainable`) THEN `by` `two months`
           IF `my impairment has become fully ascertainable` THEN `by` (`the later of` (`the date` 1 `months after` `the day it became fully ascertainable`) `and` `two months`)
           OTHERWISE `one month after my impairment becomes fully ascertainable, and not before two months after my particulars` `two months`
    WHERE
        `two months` MEANS `the date` 2 `months after` `the day I gave the insurer all relevant particulars`

-- s 282(3) "The insurer is not entitled to delay the determination of a claim under this Division on the ground that any
-- particulars about the claim are insufficient unless the insurer requested further relevant particulars within 2 weeks
-- after the claimant provided particulars." Where the request was in time the text only lifts the bar; whether the
-- particulars are insufficient is not decided here (fork F6).
@export May the insurer delay deciding my lump sum or damages claim because my particulars are insufficient (s 282(3))?
GIVEN `the day I provided my particulars` IS A DATE @desc The day you provided particulars of the claim to the insurer
      `the insurer asked me for further particulars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer asked you for further relevant particulars
      `the day it asked` IS A DATE @desc The day of that request (any day if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May the insurer delay for insufficient particulars` MEANS
    IF     `the insurer asked me for further particulars`
       AND `the day it asked` `is on or before` (`the date` 14 `days after` `the day I provided my particulars`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: the "unless" is met; whether the particulars are in fact insufficient is not settled by the text)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Notice before my weekly payments stop or go down (ss 80, 84)`

-- s 80(1) "An insurer must not discontinue payment to a worker of weekly payments of compensation, or reduce the amount
-- of the compensation, unless the required period of notice ... has expired." (2) "only if the worker has received weekly
-- payments for a continuous period of at least 12 weeks." (3) 3 months for a decision "on the basis of any reassessment
-- ... resulting from a work capacity decision". (4) otherwise "(a) ... less than 1 year -- 2 weeks, or (b) ... 1 year or
-- more -- 6 weeks." (6) (1) does not apply to a change "as a result only of the application of different rates of
-- compensation after the expiration of earlier periods of incapacity for which higher rates were payable", but notice
-- must be given before that period expires. The continuous period is measured to the day the notice is given (fork F7).
DECLARE `Notice I must get` IS ONE OF
    `no required period, as I have had weekly payments for less than 12 weeks in a row`
    `notice before the higher-rate period ends, but no required period`
    `3 months`
    `6 weeks`
    `2 weeks`

GIVEN `the day this run of weekly payments began` IS A DATE
      `the day of the notice` IS A DATE
      `the decision rests on a work capacity decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is only the step down to a lower rate when a higher-rate period ends` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Notice I must get`
`the notice required, run from` `the day this run of weekly payments began` `notice on` `the day of the notice` `work capacity` `the decision rests on a work capacity decision` `step down` `it is only the step down to a lower rate when a higher-rate period ends` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (`the days from` `the day this run of weekly payments began` `to` `the day of the notice`) LESS THAN 84
           THEN `no required period, as I have had weekly payments for less than 12 weeks in a row`
           IF `it is only the step down to a lower rate when a higher-rate period ends`
           THEN `notice before the higher-rate period ends, but no required period`
           IF `the decision rests on a work capacity decision`
           THEN `3 months`
           IF (`the date` 1 `years after` `the day this run of weekly payments began`) `is on or before` `the day of the notice`
           THEN `6 weeks`
           OTHERWISE `2 weeks`

-- The day the required period expires: the period starts when the notice is given, so it ends n days or n months later.
GIVEN `the notice` IS A `Notice I must get`, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the end of` `the notice` `from` `the start` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the notice`
    WHEN `3 months` THEN JUST (`the date` 3 `months after` `the start`)
    WHEN `6 weeks` THEN JUST (`the date` 42 `days after` `the start`)
    WHEN `2 weeks` THEN JUST (`the date` 14 `days after` `the start`)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

@export How much notice must the insurer give me before stopping or reducing my weekly payments (s 80)?
GIVEN `the day this run of weekly payments began` IS A DATE @desc The first day of the continuous period in which you have been receiving weekly payments
      `the day of the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day the insurer gave you notice that it will stop or reduce your weekly payments (or today, if you are checking ahead)
      `the decision rests on a work capacity decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision comes from the insurer reassessing your entitlement after a work capacity decision
      `it is only the step down to a lower rate when a higher-rate period ends` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the change is only the move to a lower rate because an earlier period of incapacity with a higher rate has ended (for example after the first 13 weeks)
GIVETH A `Notice I must get`
`How much notice must I get before my payments stop` MEANS
    `the notice required, run from` `the day this run of weekly payments began` `notice on` `the day of the notice` `work capacity` `the decision rests on a work capacity decision` `step down` `it is only the step down to a lower rate when a higher-rate period ends`

@export From what day may the insurer stop or reduce my weekly payments after giving me notice (s 80(1))?
GIVEN `the day this run of weekly payments began` IS A DATE @desc The first day of the continuous period in which you have been receiving weekly payments
      `the day of the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day the insurer gave you the notice of discontinuation or reduction
      `the decision rests on a work capacity decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision comes from a reassessment after a work capacity decision
      `it is only the step down to a lower rate when a higher-rate period ends` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the change is only the move to a lower rate because a higher-rate period has ended
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`From when may my payments be stopped` MEANS
    `the end of` (`the notice required, run from` `the day this run of weekly payments began` `notice on` `the day of the notice` `work capacity` `the decision rests on a work capacity decision` `step down` `it is only the step down to a lower rate when a higher-rate period ends`) `from` `the day of the notice`
    -- NOTHING where s 80(1) gives no required period: NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 80(2) and (6))

-- s 84(3) the worker may recover "(a) if no period of notice has been given -- an amount that is equal to the amount of
-- compensation ... that would have been payable during the required period of notice if payment ... had not been
-- discontinued or ... reduced, or (b) if less than the required period of notice has been given -- ... during the balance
-- of the required period". The weekly difference is spread over the days short at one seventh a day (fork F8).
@export How much can I recover from the insurer if it stopped or cut my weekly payments without the full notice (s 84)?
GIVEN `the day this run of weekly payments began` IS A DATE @desc The first day of the continuous period in which you had been receiving weekly payments
      `I was given notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer gave you any notice of the discontinuation or reduction
      `the day of the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day of that notice (any day if none)
      `the day the payments were stopped or cut` IS A DATE @desc The first day for which you were not paid, or paid less
      `the decision rests on a work capacity decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision came from a reassessment after a work capacity decision
      `it is only the step down to a lower rate when a higher-rate period ends` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the change was only the move to a lower rate because a higher-rate period had ended
      `my weekly payment before` IS A NUMBER @desc Your weekly payment before the change, in dollars
      `my weekly payment after` IS A NUMBER @desc Your weekly payment after the change, in dollars (0 if stopped)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What can I recover for short notice` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the end of` `the notice` `from` `the period start`
    WHEN JUST `the end` THEN (`my weekly payment before` MINUS `my weekly payment after`) TIMES (max 0 (`the days from` `the day the payments were stopped or cut` `to` `the end`)) DIVIDED BY 7
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0
    WHERE
        `the period start` MEANS
            IF `I was given notice`
            THEN `the day of the notice`
            ELSE `the day the payments were stopped or cut`
        `the notice` MEANS `the notice required, run from` `the day this run of weekly payments began` `notice on` `the period start` `work capacity` `the decision rests on a work capacity decision` `step down` `it is only the step down to a lower rate when a higher-rate period ends`
